# K03 S6 (Codex K03-CALLABLE-PATH-20261007-25, answer (c)): a path that selects a callable with a formal, written alone
# as a statement, is its application with no argument, refused as `Holder\viaPath()` is: the missing argument, said at
# the path.
Holder:
    fn: viaPath
end: Holder
fn: viaPath (int: n) int
    return: n + 1
end: viaPath
fn: run () int
    Holder\viaPath
    return: 7
end: run
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: run(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
